--- !u!1001 &2956635750444360287
PrefabInstance:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  serializedVersion: 2
  m_Modification:
    serializedVersion: 3
    m_TransformParent: {fileID: 217419358689457590}
    m_Modifications:
    - target: {fileID: 2116517601969916342, guid: 183e809bca3827e41a67b7345a91f0c2, type: 3}
      propertyPath: m_text
      value: 'While commonly believed to be the instigator of the crash, the extremely
        lackluster release of E.T. the Extra-Terrestrial (1982) did not create the
        crash by itself. Multiple factors had led to the economic crash of video
        games, and the public shunning of video games: Oversaturation as a result
        of too many low-quality games, extremely lackluster or non-existent quality
        standards, a lack of industry innovation, a lack of control publishers had
        over their video games/IPs, and personal computers starting to increase in
        popularity that had more than just video games.


        Consequently, video
        game companies would abandon the industry entirely or turn to personal computers,
        which had trended at the time.  The release of E.T. is a grim reminder of
        the consequences of rushing the development of a video game.'
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
    - target: {fileID: 2116517601969916342, guid: 183e809bca3827e41a67b7345a91f0c2, type: 3}
      propertyPath: m_fontSize
      value: 0.05
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
    - target: {fileID: 2116517601969916342, guid: 183e809bca3827e41a67b7345a91f0c2, type: 3}
      propertyPath: m_fontSizeBase
      value: 0.05
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
    - target: {fileID: 3395319288993390409, guid: 183e809bca3827e41a67b7345a91f0c2, type: 3}
      propertyPath: m_Name
      value: Plaque_ET_BuildupCrash
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
    - target: {fileID: 7335251674763361211, guid: 183e809bca3827e41a67b7345a91f0c2, type: 3}
      propertyPath: m_SizeDelta.x
